## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: ilo, Language: Iloko, Number of verses: 21
## References: Coloma, S. M., Nonato, M. G. M., Guzman, S. E. M., Ragudos, H. T., Leung, L. T., & Ramos, J. K. R. (2024). Simplifying Language Translation: Implementing Transliteration for Ilokano-English Declarative Sentences Using a Context-Free Grammar Approach. ; Reid, L. A. (2002). Review of Ilocano Dictionary and Grammar: Ilocano-English, English-Ilocano, by Carl Ralph Galvez Rubino. Oceanic Linguistics, 41(1). ; Rubino, C. R. G. (2000). Ilocano Dictionary and Grammar: Ilocano-English, English-Ilocano. University of Hawai'i Press.

